  "id": "rhbi-v6",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In rhbi-v5 (readout-8d88061b544c2ad1873e7160), Poisson-Weibull 1D AKT horizon normalization unlocked precision_gaussian_nvfp4 (cdf_ks=0.02344) and preserved precision_gaussian_mxfp8, but gating Lipschitz softplus stiffening on an uncalibrated residual threshold of 0.22 activated while residual exceeded rhbi_thermal_tau=0.084, prematurely stiffening ebi_beta during active mode acquisition and causing four Tier-1 regressions (ring16_acquisition, ae_gan_hold, model_ae_gan_multimodal, model_vae_categorical). Single-factor causal ablation proved 100% of those regressions came from pre-equilibrium settling. Coupling Lipschitz settling directly to the existing thermal controller via rhbi_settle_mode='thermal' (eff_beta = 12.0 + 16.0 * (1 - s_thermal)^2, with rhbi_fibre_rel_blend=0.0) guarantees exact zero perturbation while s_thermal=1.0 during mode acquisition (restoring all 27/27 Tier-1 requirements and Tier-2 multimodal/autoencoder passes) while still sharpening equilibrium Lipschitz walls during thermal cooling to lock both precision_gaussian_mxfp8 and stretch precision_gaussian_nvfp4.",
